    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "## Scope / traceability\n\nSocial Combat Chat 03, continuation after [Draft PR #438](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/pull/438) (03A isolated lifecycle) received independent `PASS_STATIC_REVIEW` on exact HEAD `add6039f288386a61b371d1a8899fb7a8209fc2d`. Canonical [Notion Chat plan](https://app.notion.com/p/3fa815ae752f810187b9eeeabdab6d2b), approved [Chat 01 spec](https://app.notion.com/p/3fb815ae752f81d1ad64cee4f5ae9ce1). **No production deployment or merge authorized by this issue.** Chat 03A PR remains Draft/unmerged; begin implementation only after integration gate.\n\n## Evidence-based backend audit, 2026-10-17\n\nThis repository already contains a deployed **Cloudflare Worker + D1** stack at `telemetry-receiver/`, with `src/worker.js`, `migrations/0001_init.sql`, `0002_session_metadata.sql`, and tests; `AsyncScene/Web/telemetry-config.js` enables the receiver endpoint. **This is telemetry infrastructure, not trusted gameplay persistence.** It accepts pseudonymous IDs without authenticated player identity; privacy minimization explicitly bans storing player-authored text; D1 telemetry rows are removed on a 30-day retention schedule and the ingress schema permits only limited behavioral events. Therefore do NOT write battle snapshots, secret commits, player-authored lines, or receipts to `telemetry_events`, or modify telemetry retention/API/owner token as a shortcut. Existing D1 confirms platform feasibility, *not* gameplay authorization.\n\nCloudflare [D1 `batch()` docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/worker-api/d1-database/) say batches are transactions and roll back on statement failure. This alone does not implement version CAS: a zero-row `UPDATE WHERE version=?` is not a SQL failure. Demonstrate atomic fencing and rollback explicitly under concurrency.\n\n## Decision gate before coding\n\n1. Select authoritative **gameplay** persistence location and retention/privacy/backup policy: recommendation to reuse the already adopted **Cloudflare Workers + D1 provider**, but isolate gameplay identity, schema, secrets, data and retention from private-alpha telemetry. A separate, explicitly provisioned **gameplay database** is an *authoritative game store*, not a second localStorage copy; this choice requires approval before provisioning. Alternative is an existing verified gameplay store, if found. **Do not claim telemetry D1 is an approved game store.**\n2. Specify player identification and authentication/authorization including reconnect, second device, impersonation, system-only actions. Anonymous telemetry IDs cannot authenticate PvP.\n3. Specify source of trusted clock and immutable signed/validated `seed`, `rulesVersion`, participant roles/snapshots/commit deadlines. Constrain use of mafia `k` until V12 gate approved.\n4. Lock immutable Chat 03A event and command contracts at a reviewed SHA and merge only under project's explicit PR integration procedure.\n\n## Candidate atomic Chat 03B deliverable (after gates)\n\n- A *single authoritative* persistence adapter for the pure Chat 03A state machine, not another client-side store.\n- Model `battles(battleId PK, version, stateJson, status, timestamps)`; `command_receipts(battleId,commandId PK-with-battleId, fingerprint, outcome, committedVersion)`; `outbox(eventId PK, battleId, version, type, payload, publishedAt?)`, or an equivalent proven schema. Separate private internal snapshots from participant views.\n- At each command: authenticate actual participant/system actor, load trusted battle/snapshot, supply trusted clock, run pure lifecycle, persist new state+receipt+outbox **atomically if stored version matches expected**. On CAS conflict reload and retry/replay deterministically. Reject replay of changed command body. Guard exactly one `battleId:final`.\n- Avoid leaking secret selections in GETs or transport events before both commits. Persist restoreable state across reload, disconnect and multiple devices. Do not trust client `actorId`, `role`, `at`, `seed`, `version` or snapshot provenance.\n- Existing legacy `Game.__S`, Stage7.15 localStorage, Events, economy, UI, NPC, vote and territory paths are **out of scope**; Stage7.15 remains PAUSED.\n- DRAW and genuine hand-edited non-DRAW both require a later Chat 05 recognition/vote gate per Chat 01; the Chat03A `finalize` must never bypass it. Mafia V12 conflict is separately gated.\n\n## Required executable acceptance\n\n1. A+B commit in either order; reveal after both despite deadline, no earlier leakage.\n2. Two concurrent commands from the same version: **only one commits**; losing command reloads/retries without lost updates.\n3. Duplicate `commandId` same payload and changed server time returns original receipt; different payload is rejected.\n4. Process crashes after DB commit / before HTTP response: retry returns original eventIds, no repeat settlement.\n5. Network disconnect, tab reload, different device/session, timeout/no-show, delayed reveal: <redacted>\n6. One stable outbox `<battleId>:final`, exactly-once durable event identity; consumer dedup by eventId; no rewards or economy mutations at this stage.\n7. Malicious actors cannot impersonate A/B/system, override snapshots/time/roles, or access hidden selections.\n8. Migration/rollback/retention, production privacy boundaries, test concurrency with a real D1 or D1-compatible isolated test harness. Mock-only CAS acceptance is insufficient.\n9. Record exact PR HEAD, Web/docs parity if relevant, dedicated Node integration CI, and no Safari/runtime acceptance until user tests.\n\n**Status:** `CHAT03B_DESIGN_GATE / NOT_IMPLEMENTED`. Do not create second active PR that overlaps unmerged #438 until ownership/integration is resolved.\n",
